body:
ASK C — BACKLOG DESIGN: work-item layer, feature branches, persona review. DESIGN FIRST (lead + designer/advocate proposal pass BEFORE implementation). NOT next. ONE concern (the design).

SHAPE:
1. each WORK ITEM is committed to a FEATURE BRANCH, in addition to its own worktree (#473 / D48 / D49);
2. any seat ASSIGNED to a work item can VIEW its worktree/branch (collaboration);
3. DECOUPLE queue items from work items — one work item may own MULTIPLE queue items (the work item is the "user story"; queue items are concrete delegated tasks);
4. the branch enables BRANCH REVIEW by one or more seats, each as a different PERSONA (domain / security / documentation expert — maps onto qa/auditor/advocate/designer).
RELATES TO: #473 worktree lifecycle, D48/D49, D50 item-scoped commits, the Router queue tools.
FLOW: recommend a DESIGN/PROPOSAL pass (lead + designer/advocate) BEFORE implementation.
ACCEPTANCE: a recorded design proposal (shape + the seam/contract + how it preserves the one-store/one-broker invariants); then implementation items if adopted.
CONSTRAINTS: one concern (the design); native Windows only; never push/publish.
